  <notes>Printed page 310 at the top. The entries are set in a narrow italic column and may be marginal annotations, but they are transcribed here as the column they stand in. The first entry's "exercituū" and the "unit" of the Hayn entry are doubtful, as is "cui" in the last entry. The stray mark above "Mors D. Nicolai" is not a letter and is not transcribed. The years are printed beside each group, not beside each line; they are attached to the first name of their group. The year 1630 is printed with a worn final figure and may read 163o; 1632 is printed with a worn final figure and may read 163z. The catchword "Berens" is partly worn.</notes>
